{"protocol": "stargate_oft", "file": "OFTCore.sol", "lines": "_toSD: return uint64(_amountLD / decimalConversionRate), constructor sets rate=10^(localDec-sharedDec)", "source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/LayerZero-Labs/LayerZero-v2/main/packages/layerzero-v2/evm/oapp/contracts/oft/OFTCore.sol", "invariant": "toSD_uint64_overflow_at_rate1_boundary", "result": "sat", "status": "CANDIDATE", "class": "overflow_truncation", "witness": "x=18446744073709551616, toSD=18446744073709551616, uint64_max=18446744073709551615, would truncate to 0", "notes": "SHARP: When localDecimals==sharedDecimals, rate=1, _toSD(x)=uint64(x) truncates any x > uint64_max. For an 18-decimal token with sharedDecimals=18, this occurs above 18.4 * 10^18 = ~18 tokens. High-supply tokens (e.g., 10^9 tokens * 10^18 = 10^27 total supply) would SILENTLY LOSE TOKENS. Note: sharedDecimals() defaults to 6 in OFTCore, so rate=1 only happens if overridden. But the constructor ALLOWS localDecimals==sharedDecimals. This is a KNOWN design consideration but the overflow is silent (no revert)."}
